Hi Thibaut, and for future users,
I have found that the package poppr, which is highly compatable with adegenet, has a useful function for saving genind objects as csv files in genalex format. Genalex format can be converted to genepop and structure format at the flick of a swtich with the free GenAlex add on in Excel, and this add on has several handy features of it?s own.
Of course Thibaut is right, and R is a highly universal and wonderfully flexible program, but hopefully this info will help others to move outside of R if they need or prefer to.
Many thanks again for your help,
Robert
